Norma in-tree fork provenance
=============================

This directory contains the runtime library source and regression tests from
Norma v0.4.11.

Upstream source:
  Project: https://github.com/BaaRai/Norma
  Canonical module path at that release: github.com/Autumn-27/norma
  Release: v0.4.11
  Commit: facbfad0e8dcfaa4015522ced21290b148f8a61f
  License: Apache License 2.0 (preserved verbatim in LICENSE)

The v0.4.11 source distribution did not contain an upstream NOTICE file. This
NOTICE records ARTEX's provenance and modifications; it does not alter the
Apache License 2.0 terms.

Included source:
  agentcore, compaction, coordinator, harness, hook, llm, mcp, memory, noa,
  noaadapter, permission, plan, skill, subagent, tool, and transcript packages,
  including their upstream regression tests and platform-specific files.

Intentionally excluded:
  - cmd/agentcore and examples/, which are standalone command/demo binaries and
    are not part of ARTEX's in-process SDK runtime.
  - the upstream go.mod and go.sum, because this fork belongs to the ARTEX root
    module rather than a nested module.
  - upstream VCS/editor metadata and the upstream repository README.

ARTEX fork modifications:
  - Rewrote Norma self-imports to
    github.com/Autumn-27/artex/internal/norma/<subpackage>.
  - Added typed, JSON-persistent opaque ProviderState on llm.Message and
    StreamEvent, plus SEProviderState.
  - Added Accumulator ownership isolation and Reset behavior for provider state.
  - Preserved state through intact API/NOA projections, cloned NOA raw data,
    and discarded state whenever projection removes or rewrites its source turn.
  - Prevented built-in Anthropic, OpenAI Chat Completions, and OpenAI Responses
    wire encoders from forwarding ProviderState, while retaining existing
    Anthropic thinking/redacted-thinking and Gemini thought signatures.
  - Clarified that Provider.Complete returns an assembled message and that a
    provider implementation may collect mandatory upstream streaming; existing
    built-in API-key providers retain their non-streaming wire behavior.
  - Added regression coverage for transcript persistence/resume, accumulator
    alias isolation/reset, context projection, and actual outgoing built-in
    provider wire omission.
  - Routed interleaved native-provider tool-input fragments by optional tool
    call ID while preserving legacy most-recent-call delta semantics.
  - Added a wrapped-error opt-out marker for physical model-request retries and
    propagated it through stream establishment, the harness, compaction, and
    NOA overflow handling so native terminal or uncertain outcomes are not
    automatically replayed.
  - On those terminal stream errors, discarded unfinished tool-call fragments
    instead of repairing partial arguments to an empty object and executing it.

No external Norma CLI is built or used by ARTEX.
